# Purpose: Limit the Docker build context to what SwiftPM needs (manifest, lockfile, Sources, Tests).
# Inputs: Paths under server/ at `docker build` time.
# Outputs: A smaller, credential-free context; excluded paths never reach the image or its cache.
# Side effects: None. Tests/ stays in the context because the manifest declares that target directory.
.build/
.swiftpm/
.local-data/
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
scripts/
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
